window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b><i>“Step away from that crow if you value your life.” </i></b></p> <p><b><i>Not a threat, but a promise. I will happily tear them to ribbons if they dare get in my way.</i></b></p> <p><b>Prisons come in many forms. This one is made of feathers and devastation.</b></p> <p>Surviving the battle was only the first test. Now, Ayna must break free from the gods’ latest punishment while the enemy regroups, striking where it hurts most. But steel and magic won’t be enough this time. To stand a chance, she must forge risky alliances and rise stronger than before—because the fate of two kingdoms rests on her shoulders.</p> <p>Something dark is stirring in Tavras, and not even divine favor may be enough to stop it.</p> <p><b>A high-stakes, heart-racing ride, </b><b><i>Flight of Fate</i></b><b> is the electrifying fourth book in the </b><b><i>Wings of Ink</i></b><b> series—perfect for fans of </b><b><i>Quicksilver</i></b><b>, </b><b><i>From Blood and Ash</i></b><b>, and </b><b><i>A Court of Thorns and Rose.</i></b></p> <p><i>The Wings of Ink series is part of the Alcunaire!</i></p>"; 
